1
00:00:01,420 --> 00:00:10,420
General Laboratory Safety. Safety instructions produced by students and staff from the Institute for Inorganic Chemistry, Kiehl.
实验室通用安全。安全须知，由基尔无机化学研究所的学生和员工制作。

2
00:00:10,420 --> 00:00:24,050
Working laboratories poses potential risks. Therefore, there is always a laboratory supervisor present.
在实验室工作存在潜在风险。因此，始终会有一名实验室负责人在场。

3
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:28,050
His task is to ensure a safe working environment in the laboratory.
他的任务是确保实验室有一个安全的工作环境。

4
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:35,050
He is the first port of call for all problems and questions. His instructions must be followed at all times.
遇到任何问题和疑问，首先要找他。必须始终听从他的指示。

5
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:45,360
Before working the laboratory can begin, the laboratory supervisor presents an introduction of the techniques and laboratory equipment to be used.
在开始实验室工作之前，实验室负责人会介绍将要使用的技术和实验室设备。

6
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:52,360
Furthermore, he will discuss personal protective body wear, which includes safety specs and a lab coat.
此外，他还会讲解个人防护服装，包括安全眼镜和实验服。

7
00:00:52,360 --> 00:00:55,360
He makes you aware of emergency facilities.
他会让你了解应急设施。

8
00:00:56,360 --> 00:01:17,360
These include an emergency shower, the eyewash fountain, fire extinguishers, fume hoods, first aid equipment, emergency switch off buttons, the fire alarm and the emergency telephone with emergency telephone numbers.
这些设施包括紧急淋浴、洗眼器、灭火器、通风柜、急救设备、紧急断电按钮、火警报警器，以及标有紧急电话号码的紧急电话。

9
00:01:20,090 --> 00:01:27,090
He informs the laboratory workers about specific dangers and supervises precautionary methods.
他会向实验室人员告知特定的危险，并监督预防措施的执行。

10
00:01:27,090 --> 00:01:38,090
Furthermore, he ensures that there is a copy of the technical rules 526 for dangerous compounds in every laboratory and makes sure that these rules are being observed.
此外，他要确保每个实验室都有一份危险化合物技术规则 526，并确保这些规则得到遵守。

11
00:01:38,090 --> 00:01:53,090
The technical rules for dangerous substances or in brief TRGS reflect the present knowledge of technology, occupational medicine and occupational hygiene as well as other proven scientific facts for working with dangerous substances.
危险物质技术规则，简称 TRGS，反映了在使用危险物质方面技术、职业医学和职业卫生的现有知识，以及其他已被证实的科学事实。

12
00:01:53,090 --> 00:01:57,090
This includes their classification and labelling.
这包括危险物质的分类和标签。

13
00:01:57,090 --> 00:02:04,090
He also ensures that emergency plans and safety information are accessible in the laboratory in a visible place.
他还要确保应急计划和安全信息放在实验室里醒目、方便取阅的地方。

14
00:02:05,090 --> 00:02:13,090
In addition, he needs to ensure that regular testing is being performed on those pieces of equipment where this is required by law.
此外，他需要确保对法律要求定期检测的设备进行定期检测。

15
00:02:14,090 --> 00:02:23,090
Operational instructions for special equipment in the laboratory are written by the laboratory supervisor who ensures that everyone has access to them.
实验室中特殊设备的操作规程由实验室负责人编写，并由他确保每个人都能查阅。

16
00:02:23,090 --> 00:02:26,090
They indicate dangers and advise on safety precautions.
这些规程指出危险，并就安全预防措施提出建议。

17
00:02:26,090 --> 00:02:36,090
Operational instructions must be written for biological materials, hazardous chemicals and their preparation as well as for machines and other technical facilities.
必须为生物材料、危险化学品及其配制，以及机器和其他技术设施编写操作规程。

18
00:02:36,090 --> 00:02:55,090
They include area of application, danger for humans and the environment, protective measures and rules of conduct, what to do in case of any malfunctions, what to do in case of emergency and first aid, appropriate disposal, maintenance for machines and technical facilities,
规程内容包括适用范围、对人和环境的危险、防护措施和行为规则、发生任何故障时该怎么办、发生紧急情况时该怎么办以及急救、正确的处置方法、机器和技术设施的维护，

19
00:02:55,090 --> 00:02:58,090
consequences if these rules are not adhered to.
以及不遵守这些规则的后果。

20
00:02:58,090 --> 00:03:02,880
There is also the assessments of dangers.
还有危险评估。

21
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:08,880
They include dangers which may occur in laboratories and measures which can be taken to prevent these dangers.
危险评估包括实验室中可能出现的危险，以及为防止这些危险可以采取的措施。

22
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:17,910
In addition, the effect of these measures is always documented.
此外，这些措施的效果总是要记录在案。

23
00:03:17,910 --> 00:03:21,910
Last but not least, there is the safety documentation itself.
最后但同样重要的是安全文件本身。

24
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:26,910
It includes an inventory of the chemicals in the laboratory.
其中包括一份实验室化学品清单。

25
00:03:26,910 --> 00:03:34,910
In addition to this, for all chemicals, the safety forms must be accessible in the laboratory.
除此之外，所有化学品的安全数据表都必须能在实验室里查阅到。

26
00:03:34,910 --> 00:03:40,910
This was an enormous amount of information which needs to sink in.
信息量真是太大了，需要好好消化一下。

27
00:03:40,910 --> 00:03:43,910
Let's look at a few real-life examples.
我们来看几个真实的例子。

28
00:03:43,910 --> 00:03:55,950
Before the lab course starts, this is Adams.
在实验课开始之前，这位是 Adams。

29
00:03:55,950 --> 00:03:58,950
And this one here, let's call him Smithy.
还有这一位，我们就叫他 Smithy 吧。

30
00:03:58,950 --> 00:04:04,670
Both are in their first year and study chemistry.
两人都是一年级学生，学的是化学。

31
00:04:05,670 --> 00:04:09,670
After university, Adams is planning to work in a large chemical company.
大学毕业后，Adams 打算去一家大型化工公司工作。

32
00:04:09,670 --> 00:04:18,670
Ideally, in research and development, Smithy thinks more about becoming an alchemist and is considering gold production.
最好是在研发部门。Smithy 想得更多的是当一名炼金术士，正在考虑炼金。

33
00:04:18,670 --> 00:04:23,670
Both still have a long way to go because beforehand they need to study.
两人都还有很长的路要走，因为在那之前他们得先学习。

34
00:04:23,670 --> 00:04:31,860
Don't we have lab course today? When is that supposed to start?
我们今天不是有实验课吗？什么时候开始？

35
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:35,860
Yes, the lab course starts in an hour. Haven't you prepared for it?
是啊，实验课一个小时后开始。你还没准备吗？

36
00:04:35,860 --> 00:04:39,860
Prepared? Why should I? They'll tell us everything.
准备？我为什么要准备？他们会把一切都告诉我们的。

37
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:41,860
Well, if you think so.
好吧，如果你这么想的话。

38
00:04:41,860 --> 00:05:04,130
Adams, what do you look like?
Adams，你这是什么打扮？

39
00:05:04,130 --> 00:05:09,130
What? Lab coats and safety specs are mandatory. Haven't you read the instructions?
什么？实验服和安全眼镜是必须穿戴的。你没看须知吗？

40
00:05:09,130 --> 00:05:13,130
But Smithy, you don't want to go into the lab like this.
可是 Smithy，你可不能就这样进实验室。

41
00:05:13,130 --> 00:05:16,630
But why ever not?
为什么不行？

42
00:05:16,630 --> 00:05:23,970
In the laboratory, you must always wear long trousers and proper covered shoes.
在实验室里，你必须始终穿长裤和合适的包脚鞋。

43
00:05:23,970 --> 00:05:26,970
However, the trousers must not be tucked inside the shoes.
不过，裤腿不能塞进鞋子里。

44
00:05:26,970 --> 00:05:34,970
No loose hair, head scarves are okay, but only if they are 100% cotton.
不能披散头发，可以戴头巾，但前提是头巾必须是 100% 纯棉的。

45
00:05:34,970 --> 00:05:38,970
If you have problems with vision, contact lenses are not suitable.
如果你视力有问题，隐形眼镜是不合适的。

46
00:05:38,970 --> 00:05:40,970
Glasses are better.
框架眼镜更好。

47
00:05:40,970 --> 00:05:43,970
What's required of women is also true for Smithy.
对女士的要求同样适用于 Smithy。

48
00:05:43,970 --> 00:05:47,970
No nylon tights, no skirts.
不穿尼龙连裤袜，不穿裙子。

49
00:05:47,970 --> 00:05:56,250
In addition, students must inform the laboratory supervisor about pregnancy and chronic illnesses.
此外，学生必须告知实验室负责人自己是否怀孕或患有慢性病。

50
00:05:56,250 --> 00:06:14,220
For example, epilepsy.
比如癫痫。

51
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:18,220
Hey, Smithy, what does that green sign tell you?
嘿，Smithy，那个绿色标志告诉你什么？

52
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:21,220
No idea. It's probably not important.
不知道。大概不重要吧。

53
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:26,220
Wrong, Smithy. This can be very important in an emergency.
错了，Smithy。这在紧急情况下可能非常重要。

54
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:56,940
Every sign has a specific meaning.
每个标志都有特定的含义。

55
00:06:56,940 --> 00:06:59,940
This stuff has an incredible colour.
这东西的颜色真不可思议。

56
00:06:59,940 --> 00:07:04,940
What are you doing? Potassium dichromate is mega dangerous. Do you want to poison us all?
你在干什么？重铬酸钾超级危险。你想把我们都毒死吗？

57
00:07:04,940 --> 00:07:07,940
Poison? How do you know?
毒？你怎么知道？

58
00:07:07,940 --> 00:07:10,940
You can tell by looking at the danger symbols.
看危险符号就知道了。

59
00:07:10,940 --> 00:07:12,940
The what?
什么符号？

60
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:16,940
Every chemical compound is labelled with danger symbols.
每种化合物都标有危险符号。

61
00:07:16,940 --> 00:07:20,940
These advise the chemists on the danger of the material.
它们提醒化学工作者注意这种物质的危险。

62
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:24,940
A detailed explanation of the different symbols will follow later.
稍后会详细讲解各种不同的符号。

63
00:07:24,940 --> 00:07:31,940
We'll go and get some concentrated hydrochloric acid.
我们去拿一些浓盐酸。

64
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:35,940
Smithy, wear gloves in case you spill something.
Smithy，戴上手套，以防你洒出什么东西。

65
00:07:35,940 --> 00:07:40,420
Not all gloves are the same.
手套也不都是一样的。

66
00:07:40,420 --> 00:07:43,420
For handling chemicals, there are different types.
处理化学品有不同类型的手套。

67
00:07:43,420 --> 00:07:50,420
These are an important means for chemists to protect their skin from coming into contact with chemical compounds.
手套是化学工作者保护皮肤、避免接触化合物的一种重要手段。

68
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:59,850
OK, this has to stir for one hour now.
好了，现在这个要搅拌一个小时。

69
00:07:59,850 --> 00:08:02,850
One hour? Well, then I'm going to eat something.
一个小时？那我去吃点东西。

70
00:08:02,850 --> 00:08:09,100
Eating in the laboratory, Smithy? That's an absolute no-no.
在实验室里吃东西，Smithy？这是绝对不允许的。

71
00:08:09,100 --> 00:08:13,100
Chemical reagents in food are not tasty for chemists.
食物里的化学试剂，对化学工作者来说可不好吃。

72
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:18,100
In addition, keeping food and drinks in the laboratory is also forbidden.
此外，在实验室里存放食物和饮料也是禁止的。

73
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:22,100
The correct handling of chemical apparatus.
正确使用化学仪器。

74
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:27,100
Adams, look. Over here I didn't have a clamp, so I just used a clothes pick.
Adams，你看。这里我没有夹子，所以就用了个晾衣夹。

75
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:31,100
I didn't have a stirrer hot plate, so I turned the toaster onto full power.
我没有搅拌加热板，所以就把烤面包机开到了最大功率。

76
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:33,100
I'll do the stirring by hand.
我就用手来搅拌吧。

77
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:36,100
And the cooling hoses are leaking a little bit.
冷却软管有一点漏水。

78
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:39,100
But it doesn't matter, because the fume hood has a drain.
不过没关系，因为通风柜有排水口。

79
00:08:41,630 --> 00:08:44,630
I'm beginning to think that you're a little bit crazy.
我开始觉得你有点疯了。

80
00:08:44,630 --> 00:08:46,630
Haven't you learned anything?
你什么都没学到吗？

81
00:08:46,630 --> 00:08:57,400
When a chemical apparatus is assembled and used, special care must be taken.
组装和使用化学仪器时，必须特别小心。

82
00:08:57,400 --> 00:09:03,400
When doing this, there's no need to be creative, and improvisations are not welcome.
在这样做的时候，不需要什么创意，也不欢迎即兴发挥。

83
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:09,400
The apparatus needs to be well constructed with no tension, and it needs to be stable.
仪器需要搭建得牢靠，没有应力，而且需要稳固。

84
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:13,400
Every apparatus requires a pressure vent.
每套仪器都需要一个泄压口。

85
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:20,400
You must not assemble a closed apparatus, because this may lead to a dangerous surge in pressure.
不得组装封闭的仪器，因为这可能导致危险的压力骤增。

86
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:23,400
Electrical equipment must be tested regularly.
电气设备必须定期检测。

87
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:28,400
High temperatures and flammable solvents are a dangerous combination.
高温和易燃溶剂是危险的组合。

88
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:34,400
Therefore, the solvent must be retained by a reflux condenser.
因此，必须用回流冷凝器把溶剂留住。

89
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:39,400
An aqua mobile indicates a working cooling process.
水流指示器表明冷却过程正常运行。

90
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:43,400
Cooling hoses with cooling water must be secured.
通冷却水的冷却软管必须固定好。

91
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:50,400
Flammable and thermally unstable compounds must not be heated over an open flame.
易燃和热不稳定的化合物不得在明火上加热。

92
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:56,400
The heat source must be easily and quickly removable from the apparatus.
热源必须能够方便、快速地从仪器上移开。

93
00:09:56,400 --> 00:10:00,400
Boiling retardation can be avoided by stirring.
搅拌可以避免暴沸。

94
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:04,900
Heating baths must be positioned safely.
加热浴必须放置稳妥。

95
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:07,900
Hot oil can lead to severe burns.
热油会造成严重烫伤。

96
00:10:07,900 --> 00:10:12,900
The maximum temperature of the oil bath must be taken into consideration.
必须考虑油浴的最高温度。

97
00:10:12,900 --> 00:10:18,150
Even laboratory glass can be dangerous.
即使是实验室玻璃器皿也可能有危险。

98
00:10:18,150 --> 00:10:24,150
Hot glass looks exactly like cold glass and can lead to burns.
热玻璃看起来和冷玻璃一模一样，可能会造成烫伤。

99
00:10:24,150 --> 00:10:29,150
Glass is very fragile, and shards of glass can cause cuts.
玻璃非常易碎，玻璃碎片会造成割伤。

100
00:10:35,180 --> 00:10:39,180
The cooling of a reaction may be performed with various techniques.
反应的冷却可以用各种方法进行。

101
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:49,180
With ice, a mixture of ice and rock salt, or with cooling mixtures consisting of dry ice or liquid nitrogen with various solvents.
用冰、冰和粗盐的混合物，或者用干冰或液氮与各种溶剂组成的冷却混合物。

102
00:10:49,180 --> 00:10:56,180
Here, you must take precautions that you choose the correct vessel and pay attention to using safety equipment.
这时你必须注意选择正确的容器，并注意使用安全装备。

103
00:10:56,180 --> 00:10:58,180
Generally, duers are suitable.
一般来说，杜瓦瓶是合适的。

104
00:10:58,180 --> 00:11:04,180
Liquid nitrogen and liquid helium belong to the ultra-low temperature coolants.
液氮和液氦属于超低温冷却剂。

105
00:11:04,180 --> 00:11:13,180
In the liquid state, they have temperatures of minus 196 degrees centigrade to minus 269 degrees centigrade.
在液态下，它们的温度为零下 196 摄氏度到零下 269 摄氏度。

106
00:11:13,180 --> 00:11:17,180
Direct skin contact may lead to severe frostbite.
皮肤直接接触可能导致严重冻伤。

107
00:11:17,180 --> 00:11:26,180
Therefore, low temperature protection gloves, safety goggles, or in some cases a face shield, must be worn when handling these coolants.
因此，处理这些冷却剂时，必须戴低温防护手套、安全护目镜，有时还要戴面罩。

108
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:30,180
When decanting, sufficient air flow must be ensured.
倾倒分装时，必须确保足够的空气流通。

109
00:11:30,180 --> 00:11:36,180
It is forbidden to remain in the elevator when ultra-cold gases are being transported.
运输超低温气体时，禁止人员留在电梯里。

110
00:11:36,180 --> 00:11:43,180
Containers must be moved with care and should never be fully closed, thus avoiding a pressure increase.
容器必须小心搬运，绝不应完全密闭，以避免压力升高。

111
00:11:43,180 --> 00:11:50,180
A danger exists in that oxygen from the air condenses in gases at ultra-low temperatures.
存在一种危险，即空气中的氧气会在超低温气体中冷凝。

112
00:11:50,180 --> 00:11:53,180
Oxygen is a strong oxidant.
氧气是一种强氧化剂。

113
00:11:53,180 --> 00:12:11,820
Therefore, there must be no flammable compounds in this container, and the workspace must be free of sources of ignition.
因此，这个容器里绝不能有可燃化合物，工作区也必须没有点火源。

114
00:12:11,820 --> 00:12:14,820
Chemical apparatus may be used under a partial vacuum.
化学仪器可以在部分真空下使用。

115
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:22,820
A partial vacuum is used, for example, for distillations and drying processes in desiccators.
例如，蒸馏和在干燥器中进行干燥时就要使用部分真空。

116
00:12:22,820 --> 00:12:28,820
Damaged glassware cannot withstand the partial vacuum and may implode.
有损伤的玻璃器皿无法承受部分真空，可能会发生内爆。

117
00:12:28,820 --> 00:12:33,820
Therefore, all glassware must be examined for cracks before use.
因此，所有玻璃器皿在使用前都必须检查有无裂纹。

118
00:12:33,820 --> 00:12:44,820
Chemical reactions under high pressure may only be performed in suitable, certified pressure vessels, which are called autoclaves.
高压下的化学反应只能在合适的、经过认证的压力容器中进行，这种容器叫做高压釜。

119
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:53,820
The maximum temperature and the maximum pressure depending on the volume of the reaction mixture in the autoclave needs to be observed.
必须注意高压釜中与反应混合物体积相关的最高温度和最高压力。

120
00:12:54,820 --> 00:12:58,820
Pressurized vessels may only be opened after pressure equalization.
压力容器只能在压力平衡之后才能打开。

121
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:02,820
The experimental apparatus must be labeled accordingly.
实验装置必须相应地贴上标签。

122
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:44,620
Gases are either available in pressurized bottles or via gas connections in the fume hood.
气体要么装在压力气瓶里，要么通过通风柜中的气体接口提供。

123
00:13:44,620 --> 00:13:48,620
A color-coding system shows you the properties of the content.
颜色编码系统会告诉你所装气体的性质。

124
00:13:48,620 --> 00:14:00,620
Inert gases are marked in green, corrosive and toxic gases yellow, flammable gases red, and oxidizing gases blue.
惰性气体用绿色标识，腐蚀性和有毒气体用黄色，易燃气体用红色，氧化性气体用蓝色。

125
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:06,620
Oxygen bottles have a white shoulder and a blue or a gray coating.
氧气瓶的瓶肩是白色的，瓶身涂层是蓝色或灰色的。

126
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:11,620
Argon bottles have a dark green shoulder and the coating is gray.
氩气瓶的瓶肩是深绿色的，瓶身涂层是灰色的。

127
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:15,620
For hydrogen bottles, shoulder and coating are red.
氢气瓶的瓶肩和瓶身都是红色的。

128
00:14:15,620 --> 00:14:20,620
Generally, you must prevent gases from leaking into the laboratory atmosphere.
一般来说，必须防止气体泄漏到实验室空气中。

129
00:14:20,620 --> 00:14:26,620
Therefore, you may use gases only in fume cupboards and in gas-tight apparatus.
因此，只能在通风柜中和气密的仪器中使用气体。

130
00:14:26,620 --> 00:14:30,620
In pressurized gas bottles, gas is compressed.
压力气瓶中的气体是经过压缩的。

131
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:34,620
Therefore, they need to be always stored in gas bottle cupboards.
因此，它们必须始终存放在气瓶柜中。

132
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:38,620
This protects them against falling over and against high temperatures.
这可以防止它们倾倒，并防止受到高温影响。

133
00:14:38,620 --> 00:14:42,620
The gas bottle cupboards are ventilated in case of gas leakage.
气瓶柜是通风的，以防气体泄漏。

134
00:14:42,620 --> 00:14:50,620
In order to use the gas, a pressure reduction valve has to be screwed onto the main valve of the gas bottle.
要使用气体，必须把减压阀拧到气瓶的总阀上。

135
00:14:50,620 --> 00:14:56,620
In order to protect the main valve, you always need to screw a cap on top of it.
为了保护总阀，必须始终在它上面拧上保护帽。

136
00:14:56,620 --> 00:15:02,620
Gas bottles may only be transported on a gas bottle carrier.
气瓶只能用气瓶推车运输。

137
00:15:02,620 --> 00:15:04,620
Working with electrical equipment
使用电气设备

138
00:15:04,620 --> 00:15:12,500
In laboratories, electrical equipment is often used.
实验室里经常使用电气设备。

139
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:16,500
In this situation, accidents with electricity can happen.
这时就可能发生触电事故。

140
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:21,500
You should bear the following points in mind when working with electrical equipment.
使用电气设备时，你应该记住以下几点。

141
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:26,500
Electrical equipment is to be used in accordance with its intended use.
电气设备应按其预定用途使用。

142
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:35,070
Different to what you can see here, electrical equipment should be in perfect condition when you use it.
与你在这里看到的不同，使用电气设备时，它应处于完好状态。

143
00:15:35,070 --> 00:15:41,580
Settings and safety precautions must be correctly adjusted.
设置和安全防护措施必须正确调整。

144
00:15:41,580 --> 00:15:45,580
Electrical equipment that is wet must never be used.
绝不能使用受潮的电气设备。

145
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:54,580
If there is damage or malfunction, the apparatus must be switched off and a qualified electrician must be notified.
如果出现损坏或故障，必须关闭设备，并通知有资质的电工。

146
00:15:54,580 --> 00:16:01,580
It is not allowed to continue using damaged equipment and the dangers must be signposted.
不允许继续使用损坏的设备，并且必须设置标志提示危险。

147
00:16:01,580 --> 00:16:07,580
Repair work by unqualified electricians is prohibited.
禁止无资质的电工进行维修工作。

148
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:16,580
Repairs of electrical facilities and equipment may only be performed by qualified electricians.
电气设施和设备只能由有资质的电工维修。

149
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:24,620
Electronic equipment in the laboratory must be tested regularly.
实验室中的电子设备必须定期检测。

150
00:16:24,620 --> 00:16:26,620
Working with radiation
辐射工作

151
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:38,100
Smithy, I don't think we're allowed in here.
Smithy，我觉得我们不能进这里。

152
00:16:38,100 --> 00:16:42,100
You kidding? I'm a student here. Of course I'm allowed to go in there.
开什么玩笑？我是这里的学生。我当然可以进去。

153
00:16:52,740 --> 00:17:01,740
Working with ionising radiation and radioactive compounds requires a special instruction by the radiation safety officer, my dear Smithy.
亲爱的 Smithy，使用电离辐射和放射性化合物，需要接受辐射安全负责人的专门指导。

154
00:17:01,740 --> 00:17:06,740
Such work must only be performed at specially designated workplaces.
这类工作只能在专门指定的工作场所进行。

155
00:17:06,740 --> 00:17:13,740
You must limit exposure by employing technological measures to keep exposure as low as possible.
你必须通过采用技术措施来限制暴露，使暴露尽可能低。

156
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:20,740
Handling ionising radiation and radioactive chemicals is regulated by the radiation protection ordinance.
电离辐射和放射性化学品的使用受辐射防护条例的管理。

157
00:17:20,740 --> 00:17:26,740
The principal rule is, everything is forbidden unless you have special permission.
基本原则是：除非获得特别许可，否则一切都是禁止的。

158
00:17:26,740 --> 00:17:31,740
X-rays are mostly used in crystallography.
X 射线主要用于晶体学。

159
00:17:31,740 --> 00:17:39,330
There are warning signs and warning lights alerting you to the danger.
那里有警告标志和警示灯提醒你注意危险。

160
00:17:39,330 --> 00:17:47,330
The equipment may only be used with permission and only after being briefed by the radiation protection officer.
这些设备只有在获得许可、并经辐射防护负责人讲解后才能使用。

161
00:17:48,330 --> 00:17:53,330
Fully protected equipment ensures that nobody comes into contact with radiation.
全防护设备能确保任何人都不会接触到辐射。

162
00:17:53,330 --> 00:18:01,330
In this instance, x-ray suites are not controlled areas, and carrying a personal dosimeter is not required.
在这种情况下，X 射线室不属于控制区，不需要佩戴个人剂量计。

163
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:05,330
Students may use these machines after being instructed.
学生在接受指导后可以使用这些仪器。

164
00:18:05,330 --> 00:18:15,330
For work with gamma radiation, the same rules apply, but in this case a dosimeter must be worn, which is changed at regular intervals.
伽马射线工作适用同样的规则，但在这种情况下必须佩戴剂量计，剂量计要定期更换。

165
00:18:15,330 --> 00:18:23,330
Laser radiation is often being used in optical spectrometers, and as such presents a danger to the eyes.
激光辐射常用于光谱仪中，因此会对眼睛造成危险。

166
00:18:23,330 --> 00:18:28,330
An area in which lasers are being used must be labelled.
使用激光的区域必须设置标识。

167
00:18:28,330 --> 00:18:32,330
When working with lasers, special safety goggles must be worn.
使用激光时，必须佩戴专用的防护眼镜。

168
00:18:32,330 --> 00:18:38,760
The competent handling of chemicals
正确处理化学品

169
00:18:38,760 --> 00:18:44,040
Chemicals must be stored in special chemical cupboards.
化学品必须存放在专用的化学品柜中。

170
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:50,040
In all circumstances, they must be labelled by the user or by the supplier.
在任何情况下，化学品都必须由使用者或供应商贴上标签。

171
00:18:50,040 --> 00:18:56,040
A label gives information about the name and product identification,
标签提供的信息包括名称和产品标识、

172
00:18:56,040 --> 00:19:03,040
danger pictograms, H&P statements, nominal content,
危险象形图、H 和 P 说明、标称含量、

173
00:19:03,040 --> 00:19:08,040
contact information of the supplier, and a signal word, if necessary.
供应商的联系信息，以及必要时的信号词。

174
00:19:08,040 --> 00:19:13,040
Signal words are attention or danger.
信号词是“警告”或“危险”。

175
00:19:13,040 --> 00:19:21,350
In order to recognise dangers immediately, all chemicals are marked with GHS labels.
为了能立即识别危险，所有化学品都贴有 GHS 标签。

176
00:19:21,350 --> 00:19:26,350
There are altogether nine general health and safety symbols.
一共有九个通用的健康与安全符号。

177
00:19:26,350 --> 00:19:31,350
The exploding bomb signifies explosive chemicals.
爆炸的炸弹表示爆炸性化学品。

178
00:19:31,350 --> 00:19:38,350
The flame, flammable solids, liquids, aerosols and gases,
火焰表示易燃固体、液体、气溶胶和气体，

179
00:19:38,350 --> 00:19:43,350
pyrophoric compounds and organic peroxides.
自燃化合物和有机过氧化物。

180
00:19:43,350 --> 00:19:49,350
The flame above a circle signifies oxidising solids, liquids or gases.
圆圈上方的火焰表示氧化性固体、液体或气体。

181
00:19:49,350 --> 00:19:53,350
The gas bottle warns of gases under pressure.
气瓶警示加压气体。

182
00:19:53,350 --> 00:19:58,350
The corrosive effect of compounds which are corrosive for the skin
腐蚀符号表示对皮肤有腐蚀性的化合物，

183
00:19:58,350 --> 00:20:03,350
may cause severe eye damage or are corrosive with respect to metals.
可能造成严重眼损伤或对金属有腐蚀性的化合物。

184
00:20:04,350 --> 00:20:09,350
And the skull with the crossbones warns of chemicals which are acutely toxic
骷髅和交叉骨警示急性毒性

185
00:20:09,350 --> 00:20:12,350
within categories 1 to 3.
为第 1 至 3 类的化学品。

186
00:20:12,350 --> 00:20:18,350
The exclamation mark signifies chemicals with acute toxicity of category 4
感叹号表示第 4 类急性毒性的化学品，

187
00:20:18,350 --> 00:20:21,350
and skin irritating chemicals of category 2.
以及第 2 类皮肤刺激性化学品。

188
00:20:21,350 --> 00:20:25,350
The upper body with a star represents danger for your health
带星形的上半身代表对健康的危害，

189
00:20:25,350 --> 00:20:32,350
and the label is used for carcinogenic chemicals category 1a, b, 2
这个标签用于第 1A、1B、2 类致癌化学品，

190
00:20:32,350 --> 00:20:37,350
also warns of the danger of aspiration, sensibleisation of the respiratory tract
还警示吸入危害、呼吸道致敏

191
00:20:37,350 --> 00:20:40,350
and target organ toxicity.
以及特定靶器官毒性。

192
00:20:40,350 --> 00:20:46,350
Lastly, the dead fish is used to label chemicals which may harm the general environment
最后，死鱼用于标示可能危害一般环境

193
00:20:46,350 --> 00:20:51,790
or more specifically, the water environment.
或者更具体地说危害水环境的化学品。

194
00:20:51,790 --> 00:20:55,790
In addition, a detailed estimation of the danger of the chemicals
此外，可以利用 H 和 P 说明

195
00:20:55,790 --> 00:20:59,790
can be performed using the H and P statements.
对化学品的危险进行详细评估。

196
00:20:59,790 --> 00:21:03,790
The danger potential of every chemical is precisely determined
每种化学品的潜在危险都由

197
00:21:03,790 --> 00:21:07,790
by hazard statements or short H statements.
危险说明，简称 H 说明，精确确定。

198
00:21:07,790 --> 00:21:13,790
Furthermore, there are precautionary statements or short P statements
此外，还有防范说明，简称 P 说明，

199
00:21:13,790 --> 00:21:17,790
which give safety advice on dealing with the respective chemical.
就如何处理相应的化学品提供安全建议。

200
00:21:17,790 --> 00:21:23,790
H statements are characterised by the letter H and a three digit number.
H 说明以字母 H 加一个三位数字来表示。

201
00:21:23,790 --> 00:21:27,790
The first number gives the class of the H statement.
第一位数字表示 H 说明的类别。

202
00:21:27,790 --> 00:21:32,790
Two stands for physical danger, three for health hazards
2 代表物理危险，3 代表健康危害，

203
00:21:32,790 --> 00:21:35,790
and four for environmental dangers.
4 代表环境危害。

204
00:21:35,790 --> 00:21:39,790
The second and third digits are consecutive numbers.
第二位和第三位数字是连续编号。

205
00:21:39,790 --> 00:21:45,790
P statements are sorted into five groups of safety directions.
P 说明分为五组安全指示。

206
00:21:45,790 --> 00:21:53,790
One, general, two, prevention, three, reaction,
1，一般；2，预防；3，应对；

207
00:21:53,790 --> 00:21:58,790
four, storage, and five, disposal.
4，储存；5，处置。

208
00:21:58,790 --> 00:22:08,500
In order to estimate how toxic a chemical is, an LD50 value is determined.
为了估计一种化学品的毒性有多大，要测定 LD50 值。

209
00:22:08,500 --> 00:22:13,500
The LD50 value is the amount of a chemical which causes the death
LD50 值是导致一组试验动物中 50% 死亡的

210
00:22:13,500 --> 00:22:17,500
of 50% of a group of test animals.
化学品的量。

211
00:22:17,500 --> 00:22:21,500
Toxic or hazardous compounds should always be replaced
在化学反应中，只要有可能，有毒或危险的化合物

212
00:22:21,500 --> 00:22:26,500
by less toxic substances as far as this is possible in a chemical reaction.
都应该用毒性较低的物质来替代。

213
00:22:26,500 --> 00:22:34,500
For example, benzene can often be replaced by the much less toxic toluene.
例如，苯通常可以用毒性低得多的甲苯来替代。

214
00:22:34,500 --> 00:22:40,500
Experimenting with chemicals while bearing in mind the operating instructions.
在牢记操作规程的前提下用化学品做实验。

215
00:22:40,500 --> 00:22:45,500
As soon as you start an experiment, a few things need attention.
一旦开始实验，有几件事需要注意。

216
00:22:45,500 --> 00:22:50,500
All experiments must be carefully planned and prepared.
所有实验都必须精心计划和准备。

217
00:22:50,500 --> 00:22:55,500
Good preparations can be done by reading the description of the experiment
要做好准备，可以阅读实验说明

218
00:22:55,500 --> 00:23:01,500
and the operating instructions by reading the labeling of the starting materials
和操作规程，阅读起始原料

219
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:05,500
and synthesized compounds, dangers for persons and the environment,
和合成化合物的标签、对人和环境的危险、

220
00:23:05,500 --> 00:23:11,500
required safety precautions and codes of practice, behavior in case of emergency,
所需的安全预防措施和操作规范、紧急情况下的行为、

221
00:23:11,500 --> 00:23:17,500
first aid measures in case of accidents, and notes for the disposal of the chemical.
发生事故时的急救措施，以及化学品的处置说明。

222
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:22,780
Labeling of the reagents and synthesized compounds,
试剂和合成化合物的标签、

223
00:23:22,780 --> 00:23:27,780
dangers for persons and the environment, required safety precautions
对人和环境的危险、所需的安全预防措施

224
00:23:27,780 --> 00:23:31,780
and code of practice, procedure in case of emergency,
和操作规范、紧急情况下的程序、

225
00:23:31,780 --> 00:23:37,780
first aid measures in case of accidents, and notes for the disposal of the chemical.
发生事故时的急救措施，以及化学品的处置说明。

226
00:23:37,780 --> 00:23:42,780
Before you start an experiment, you must also consider if you have enough time
在开始实验之前，你还必须考虑自己是否有足够的时间

227
00:23:42,780 --> 00:23:44,780
for the entire experiment.
完成整个实验。

228
00:23:44,780 --> 00:23:48,780
If this is not the case, you must decide in advance
如果没有，你必须事先决定

229
00:23:48,780 --> 00:23:54,780
at which point the experiment can be interrupted without danger.
实验可以在哪个节点安全地中断。

230
00:23:54,780 --> 00:23:59,780
An experiment which needs to run for a longer period of time without supervision
需要在无人看管的情况下长时间运行的实验，

231
00:23:59,780 --> 00:24:03,780
needs to be placed in the designated night labs.
必须放在指定的夜间实验室里。

232
00:24:03,780 --> 00:24:07,780
You must ensure that you have all reagents and equipment
在开始实验之前，你必须确保所有试剂和设备

233
00:24:07,780 --> 00:24:10,780
ready to use before starting an experiment.
都已准备好可以使用。

234
00:24:10,780 --> 00:24:14,780
Having to search for missing items leads to a hectic rush
不得不去找缺少的东西，会导致手忙脚乱，

235
00:24:14,780 --> 00:24:20,780
and therefore to a higher safety risk, especially during difficult phases of an experiment.
从而带来更高的安全风险，尤其是在实验的困难阶段。

236
00:24:20,780 --> 00:24:25,260
I'm telling you, it was an incredibly amazing evening.
我跟你说，那是一个超级棒的晚上。

237
00:24:25,260 --> 00:24:28,260
I've never been to a birthday party as good as that.
我从来没参加过那么好的生日派对。

238
00:24:28,260 --> 00:24:32,260
This girl, blonde, long legs, all the way to the ground.
有个女孩，金发，大长腿，一直长到地上。

239
00:24:32,260 --> 00:24:36,260
Unbelievable. Really? Awesome. You should have been there.
难以置信。真的吗？太棒了。你真该去的。

240
00:24:36,260 --> 00:24:38,260
I tell you, it was fantastic.
我跟你说，太精彩了。

241
00:24:38,260 --> 00:24:42,260
Ah, yes, diluting the acid to two molar.
啊，对了，把酸稀释到 2 摩尔。

242
00:24:42,260 --> 00:24:46,260
Oh no, smithy. You know.
哎呀，不行，Smithy。你知道的。

243
00:24:46,260 --> 00:24:51,260
Acid last and not the water, otherwise it's bound to falter.
酸要最后加，不能最后加水，否则肯定要出事。

244
00:24:51,260 --> 00:24:57,260
When mixing acids and water, it is important that the water is added first
混合酸和水时，重要的是先加水，

245
00:24:57,260 --> 00:25:00,260
because otherwise a violent reaction takes place.
否则会发生剧烈反应。

246
00:25:00,260 --> 00:25:13,560
Well, this soup has to ferment now for an hour.
好了，这锅汤现在要发酵一个小时。

247
00:25:13,560 --> 00:25:17,840
I guess it's going to be okay over here as well.
我想放在这边应该也没问题。

248
00:25:17,840 --> 00:25:19,840
The fume hood is full anyway.
反正通风柜也满了。

249
00:25:19,840 --> 00:25:22,840
This tin is not really ideal.
这个罐子其实不太理想。

250
00:25:22,840 --> 00:25:24,840
And also the label is missing.
而且标签也没有。

251
00:25:24,840 --> 00:25:26,840
Ah, it'll be fine.
啊，没事的。

252
00:25:26,840 --> 00:25:29,380
Oh, oh.
哦，哦。

253
00:25:29,380 --> 00:25:35,360
Chemicals must always be stored in adequate containers,
化学品必须始终存放在合适的容器中，

254
00:25:35,360 --> 00:25:37,360
and it is vital that they are labeled.
而且贴上标签至关重要。

255
00:25:37,360 --> 00:25:40,360
They need to be kept either in the fume hood
它们需要放在通风柜里，

256
00:25:40,360 --> 00:25:42,360
or in specially designated cupboards
或者专门指定的柜子里，

257
00:25:42,360 --> 00:25:46,360
in order to prevent danger to other co-workers in the laboratory.
以免对实验室里的其他同事造成危险。

258
00:25:46,360 --> 00:25:51,360
The label must be precise so that every danger can be assessed
标签必须准确，这样即使是没有参与实验的人，

259
00:25:51,360 --> 00:25:54,360
even by a person not involved in the experiment.
也能评估出每一种危险。

260
00:25:54,360 --> 00:25:59,360
Now, even smithy and Adams know that it is better to work in a fume cupboard,
现在，就连 Smithy 和 Adams 都知道最好在通风柜里操作，

261
00:25:59,360 --> 00:26:04,360
but even here there are a few important things to take note of.
但即使在这里，也有几件重要的事情需要注意。

262
00:26:04,360 --> 00:26:10,360
The fume cupboard can only suck in the air at full capacity when it is closed.
通风柜只有在关闭时才能以最大能力抽风。

263
00:26:10,360 --> 00:26:13,360
A short demonstration illustrates this.
一个简短的演示可以说明这一点。

264
00:26:13,360 --> 00:26:21,500
Before work commences, the fume hood should be tested by the user
开始工作之前，使用者应测试通风柜，

265
00:26:21,500 --> 00:26:24,500
to check that it is functioning correctly.
检查它是否运行正常。

266
00:26:24,500 --> 00:26:27,500
Don't forget to switch the fume hood on.
别忘了打开通风柜。

267
00:26:27,500 --> 00:26:30,500
Then the experiment is placed in the fume hood
然后把实验装置放进通风柜，

268
00:26:30,500 --> 00:26:32,500
and the front screen is closed.
关上前视窗。

269
00:26:32,500 --> 00:26:37,500
It is possible to work comfortably through the side openings of the front screen.
可以通过前视窗的侧面开口舒适地操作。

270
00:26:37,500 --> 00:26:40,500
Never put your head into the fume cupboard
绝不要把头伸进通风柜里，

271
00:26:40,500 --> 00:26:44,500
because the heavy front screen can cause extreme injuries.
因为沉重的前视窗可能造成极其严重的伤害。

272
00:26:44,500 --> 00:26:48,500
If you inadvertently spill hazardous substances,
如果你不小心洒出了危险物质，

273
00:26:48,500 --> 00:26:53,500
you should only remove them and dispose of them while following certain rules.
清除和处置时只能遵循一定的规则。

274
00:26:54,500 --> 00:26:58,500
It is absolutely essential that you know the chemical
在擦拭之前，你绝对必须了解这种化学品

275
00:26:58,500 --> 00:27:01,500
and its properties before you wipe it up,
及其性质，

276
00:27:01,500 --> 00:27:05,500
because in some instances this would lead to violent reactions.
因为在某些情况下，擦拭会导致剧烈反应。

277
00:27:05,500 --> 00:27:09,500
If hazardous liquid substances have been spilt,
如果洒出的是危险液体物质，

278
00:27:09,500 --> 00:27:12,500
you must use special resins.
必须使用专用的吸附材料。

279
00:27:12,500 --> 00:27:17,130
This will help you absorb the liquid.
这能帮你吸收液体。

280
00:27:17,130 --> 00:27:21,130
If fine powders are spilt, they must be congealed with water.
如果洒出的是细粉末，必须用水润湿使其结团。

281
00:27:21,130 --> 00:27:25,130
All waste must be disposed of appropriately.
所有废物都必须妥善处置。

282
00:28:25,200 --> 00:28:33,350
Hygiene is extremely important in the laboratory.
卫生在实验室里极其重要。

283
00:28:33,350 --> 00:28:36,350
After work, hands must be washed thoroughly
工作结束后，必须彻底洗手，

284
00:28:36,350 --> 00:28:41,350
so that no chemicals from the laboratory can be transported outside.
这样就不会把实验室里的化学品带到外面。

285
00:28:41,350 --> 00:28:44,350
Working clothes, such as a lab coat,
工作服，比如实验服、

286
00:28:44,350 --> 00:28:48,350
safety goggles and so on, must be stored in the designated lockers.
安全护目镜等，必须存放在指定的储物柜里。

287
00:28:48,350 --> 00:28:51,350
These items must be worn in the lab,
这些物品必须在实验室里穿戴，

288
00:28:51,350 --> 00:28:54,350
but under no circumstances outside the laboratory,
但在任何情况下都不能穿戴到实验室外面。

289
00:28:54,350 --> 00:29:03,680
danger in the laboratory through flammable and explosive chemicals.
易燃和爆炸性化学品在实验室中造成的危险。

290
00:29:03,680 --> 00:29:09,680
In the laboratory, flammable and explosive chemicals present particular dangers.
在实验室里，易燃和爆炸性化学品会带来特殊的危险。

291
00:29:09,680 --> 00:29:13,680
Among these are solvents, alkaline metals
其中包括溶剂、碱金属

292
00:29:13,680 --> 00:29:21,680
and hydrides, silanes, nitroso and nitro compounds, azides and fulminates.
和氢化物、硅烷、亚硝基和硝基化合物、叠氮化物和雷酸盐。

293
00:29:21,680 --> 00:29:25,680
Solvents, which are often highly flammable,
溶剂往往是高度易燃的，

294
00:29:25,680 --> 00:29:28,680
require special measures for handling and storage.
在处理和储存时需要采取特殊措施。

295
00:29:28,680 --> 00:29:33,680
Overheating, proximity to flames and sparks are to be avoided.
要避免过热，避免靠近火焰和火花。

296
00:29:33,680 --> 00:29:39,680
Storage in special fire protected safety cupboards is obligatory in this case.
在这种情况下，必须储存在专门的防火安全柜中。

297
00:29:39,680 --> 00:29:44,680
Self-inflammable chemicals may ignite when in contact with air and water.
自燃化学品在接触空气和水时可能会着火。

298
00:29:44,680 --> 00:29:50,680
They are, for example, alkaline metals and hydrides and also silanes.
例如碱金属和氢化物，还有硅烷。

299
00:29:50,680 --> 00:29:54,680
Shock-sensitive chemicals carry the danger of explosion.
对冲击敏感的化学品有爆炸的危险。

300
00:29:54,680 --> 00:30:00,680
Nitroso and nitro compounds, azides and fulminates require careful handling.
亚硝基和硝基化合物、叠氮化物和雷酸盐需要小心处理。

301
00:30:00,680 --> 00:30:06,680
Shock, friction and solid inclusion must be avoided in all circumstances.
在任何情况下都必须避免冲击、摩擦和固体夹杂。

302
00:30:06,680 --> 00:30:09,680
In order to react quickly in case of fire,
为了在发生火灾时迅速作出反应，

303
00:30:09,680 --> 00:30:15,680
it is important to inform yourself about the fire extinguishers in the laboratory and how to use them.
重要的是了解实验室里的灭火器以及如何使用它们。

304
00:30:15,680 --> 00:30:18,680
The fire extinguishers you will find in the laboratory
你在实验室里看到的灭火器，

305
00:30:18,680 --> 00:30:24,680
are classified according to their extinguishing effect for different classes of fire.
是按照对不同类别火灾的灭火效果来分类的。

306
00:30:24,680 --> 00:30:30,680
ABC powder extinguishers are suitable for burning liquids, solids and gases.
ABC 干粉灭火器适用于燃烧的液体、固体和气体。

307
00:30:30,680 --> 00:30:34,680
Burning metals, however, must be extinguished using sand.
但燃烧的金属必须用沙子扑灭。

308
00:30:34,680 --> 00:30:42,680
Human bodies that are on fire can also be extinguished with a fire extinguisher or an emergency shower.
身上着火的人也可以用灭火器或紧急淋浴来灭火。

309
00:30:42,680 --> 00:30:46,680
If a fire is too large, the building must be evacuated
如果火势太大，必须撤离大楼，

310
00:30:46,680 --> 00:30:50,680
and an emergency call to the fire brigade must be made.
并拨打火警电话通知消防队。

311
00:30:50,680 --> 00:30:53,680
The fire brigade will ask the following questions
消防队会问以下问题，

312
00:30:53,680 --> 00:30:57,680
which you should answer calmly and objectively if possible.
你应尽可能冷静、客观地回答。

313
00:30:57,680 --> 00:30:59,680
Where did it happen?
在哪里发生的？

314
00:30:59,680 --> 00:31:01,680
What happened?
发生了什么？

315
00:31:01,680 --> 00:31:03,680
How many injured persons?
有多少人受伤？

316
00:31:03,680 --> 00:31:05,680
Which injuries?
受了什么伤？

317
00:31:05,680 --> 00:31:12,660
It is imperative to wait for further questions and not to terminate the call.
一定要等待对方的进一步提问，不要挂断电话。

318
00:31:12,660 --> 00:31:17,660
Danger for health through resorption of chemicals.
化学品被人体吸收对健康造成的危险。

319
00:31:17,660 --> 00:31:21,660
Hazardous substances can have a health damaging effect on the human body
危险物质由于其急性或慢性毒性作用，

320
00:31:21,660 --> 00:31:24,660
because of their acute or chronic toxic effects.
可能对人体产生损害健康的影响。

321
00:31:24,660 --> 00:31:31,660
These are, among others, corrosiveness, carcinogenic effects or teratogenous properties.
其中包括腐蚀性、致癌作用或致畸性等。

322
00:31:31,660 --> 00:31:34,660
All these factors are taken into consideration
在对化学品进行分类和标签时，

323
00:31:34,660 --> 00:31:39,660
for implementing the classification and labelling of chemicals.
所有这些因素都要考虑在内。

324
00:31:39,660 --> 00:31:43,660
Poisoning can cause several different effects on the body.
中毒会对身体造成多种不同的影响。

325
00:31:43,660 --> 00:31:53,000
Symptoms may occur suddenly, acute poisoning or gradually, chronic poisoning.
症状可能突然出现，即急性中毒，也可能逐渐出现，即慢性中毒。

326
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:57,000
Chemical compounds may be resorbed in different ways.
化合物可以通过不同的途径被吸收。

327
00:31:57,000 --> 00:32:00,000
For example, inhaling via the lungs,
例如，通过肺部吸入，

328
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:05,000
that is gases, aerosols and in general, respiratory poisons,
也就是气体、气溶胶，以及一般的呼吸毒物，

329
00:32:05,000 --> 00:32:11,000
orally via the digestive system or dermally via the skin and mucosa.
通过消化系统经口摄入，或者通过皮肤和黏膜经皮吸收。

330
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:16,000
The most common way of exposure for the human body is via inhalation.
人体最常见的暴露途径是吸入。

331
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:23,000
It is a lot simpler to prevent oral incorporation or resorption via the skin.
防止经口摄入或经皮肤吸收要简单得多。

332
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:26,000
As soon as a toxic chemical gets into the body,
有毒化学品一旦进入人体，

333
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:30,000
it is distributed via blood circulation.
就会通过血液循环分布到全身。

334
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:35,000
Irrespective of the symptoms experienced in the area of exposure,
不论暴露部位出现什么症状，

335
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:38,000
specific effects in the body occur.
体内都会产生特定的作用。

336
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:42,000
The local effect on the place of exposure of the skin or the mucosa,
在皮肤或黏膜暴露部位的局部作用，

337
00:32:42,000 --> 00:32:48,000
for example, chemical burns by bases or acids, is irreversible.
比如碱或酸造成的化学灼伤，是不可逆的。

338
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:52,000
On the other hand, the resorptive effects are often reversible
另一方面，吸收后的全身作用往往是可逆的，

339
00:32:52,000 --> 00:32:55,000
as long as countermeasures are taken in time.
只要及时采取应对措施。

340
00:32:55,000 --> 00:33:02,730
The general rule is avoid contact with dangerous substances.
一般规则是：避免接触危险物质。

341
00:33:02,730 --> 00:33:06,730
First aid in case of chemical accidents.
化学事故的急救。

342
00:33:06,730 --> 00:33:18,590
Hey, Henry, can you tell me the time?
嘿，Henry，你能告诉我现在几点吗？

343
00:33:18,590 --> 00:33:23,820
About half to 11 in Smithy.
大约差半小时十一点，Smithy。

344
00:33:23,820 --> 00:33:30,020
What? I don't understand that.
什么？我听不懂。

345
00:33:30,020 --> 00:33:32,020
Gerald, just tell me the time.
Gerald，你就告诉我几点了吧。

346
00:33:32,020 --> 00:33:34,020
In normal English, please.
请用正常的英语说。

347
00:33:34,020 --> 00:33:38,020
Almost 10.30, but Henry just told you.
快十点半了，不过 Henry 刚才已经告诉你了。

348
00:33:38,020 --> 00:33:41,020
Gerald, what's wrong with you? Say something.
Gerald，你怎么了？说话啊。

349
00:33:49,060 --> 00:33:52,060
Now it is high time for the lab supervisor to react.
现在实验室负责人必须马上作出反应了。

350
00:33:52,060 --> 00:33:57,060
He immediately proclaims an accident and asks everyone to leave the laboratory.
他立即宣布发生事故，并要求所有人离开实验室。

351
00:33:57,060 --> 00:33:59,060
Switch off gas, water and power supplies.
关闭燃气、水和电源。

352
00:33:59,060 --> 00:34:03,060
Help injured persons only if it does not put yourself in danger.
只有在不会让自己陷入危险的情况下才去帮助伤员。

353
00:34:03,060 --> 00:34:05,060
Try to keep calm.
尽量保持冷静。

354
00:34:05,060 --> 00:34:08,060
Hectic actions may cause further danger.
手忙脚乱可能造成进一步的危险。

355
00:34:08,060 --> 00:34:14,940
Thoughtful and professional action is now required.
现在需要的是深思熟虑、专业的行动。

356
00:34:14,940 --> 00:34:18,940
Make an emergency call and answer the following questions.
拨打急救电话，并回答以下问题。

357
00:34:18,940 --> 00:34:21,940
Where did it happen? What happened?
在哪里发生的？发生了什么？

358
00:34:21,940 --> 00:34:25,940
How many injured persons? Which type of injuries?
有多少人受伤？受了什么类型的伤？

359
00:34:25,940 --> 00:34:30,940
It is imperative to wait for further questions and not to terminate the call.
一定要等待对方的进一步提问，不要挂断电话。

360
00:34:30,940 --> 00:34:35,110
Be a first aider.
做一名急救员。

361
00:34:35,110 --> 00:34:41,110
Every person working in a chemical company is asked to enroll in a first aid course.
每个在化工企业工作的人都被要求参加急救课程。

362
00:34:41,110 --> 00:34:45,110
In general, you should pay attention to the following.
一般来说，你应该注意以下几点。

363
00:34:45,110 --> 00:34:50,110
Burns must be cooled with running water for at least 10 minutes.
烧烫伤必须用流水冷却至少 10 分钟。

364
00:34:50,110 --> 00:34:53,110
Fresh air must be provided.
必须提供新鲜空气。

365
00:34:53,110 --> 00:34:57,110
Exposed skin must be washed with a lot of water.
接触到化学品的皮肤必须用大量的水冲洗。

366
00:34:57,110 --> 00:35:03,110
In case of eye contact, the eyes must be washed for at least 10 minutes with the eye shower.
如果眼睛接触到化学品，必须用洗眼器冲洗眼睛至少 10 分钟。

367
00:35:03,110 --> 00:35:07,110
For this, keep the eye open with your thumb and forefinger.
冲洗时，用拇指和食指撑开眼睛。

368
00:35:07,110 --> 00:35:10,110
In emergencies, use the first aid kit.
紧急情况下，使用急救箱。

369
00:35:10,110 --> 00:35:15,110
Unconscious people must be placed on their side in the recovery position.
失去意识的人必须侧卧，摆成复苏体位。

370
00:35:15,110 --> 00:35:19,110
The body temperature of injured people must not drop.
不能让伤员的体温下降。

371
00:35:19,110 --> 00:35:24,110
Generally, all accidents must be reported to the head of the laboratory or the assistant
一般来说，所有事故都必须报告给实验室负责人或助教，

372
00:35:24,110 --> 00:35:30,320
and because of insurance issues, must always be documented.
并且由于保险方面的原因，必须始终记录在案。

373
00:35:30,320 --> 00:35:34,320
Respiratory safety guards as a life-saving process.
呼吸防护是一种救命措施。

374
00:35:34,320 --> 00:35:41,320
As we have just seen in the film, using respiratory equipment in emergencies can be life-saving.
正如我们刚才在影片中看到的，在紧急情况下使用呼吸防护设备可以救命。

375
00:35:41,320 --> 00:35:49,320
Even in the day-to-day running of the lab, there are cases where respiratory protection is important to protect your life.
即使在实验室的日常运行中，也有一些情况下呼吸防护对保护你的生命很重要。

376
00:35:49,320 --> 00:35:54,320
Air consists of 21% oxygen and 78% nitrogen.
空气由 21% 的氧气和 78% 的氮气组成。

377
00:35:54,320 --> 00:36:00,320
However, air can also contain harmful substances in gaseous or solid form,
但是，空气中也可能含有气态或固态的有害物质，

378
00:36:00,320 --> 00:36:04,320
which can be toxic even in low concentrations.
这些物质即使浓度很低也可能有毒。

379
00:36:04,320 --> 00:36:07,320
In a laboratory, such compounds are often being produced.
在实验室里，经常会产生这类化合物。

380
00:36:07,320 --> 00:36:12,320
Suitable respiratory protection is required to prevent intoxications.
需要合适的呼吸防护来防止中毒。

381
00:36:12,320 --> 00:36:17,320
This will work if the concentration of the harmful substance is not too high
如果有害物质的浓度不太高，

382
00:36:17,320 --> 00:36:20,320
or the oxygen concentration is too low.
或者氧气浓度太低，呼吸防护就能起作用。

383
00:36:20,320 --> 00:36:23,320
Even fine particle dust leads to significant dangers.
即使是细颗粒粉尘也会带来很大的危险。

384
00:36:23,320 --> 00:36:29,320
As you can see in the example, it is dispersed in the air, can be inhaled and reaches the lungs
正如你在这个例子中看到的，它分散在空气中，可以被吸入并到达肺部，

385
00:36:29,320 --> 00:36:32,320
and in the end, the cardiovascular system.
最终进入心血管系统。

386
00:36:32,320 --> 00:36:34,320
Cleaning and waste disposal.
清洁和废物处置。

387
00:36:34,320 --> 00:36:40,080
Actually, I was going to do a really exciting reaction in an hour's time,
其实我一个小时后要做一个非常激动人心的反应，

388
00:36:40,080 --> 00:36:44,080
but the flask is totally dirty and cloudy.
但是这个烧瓶脏透了，还雾蒙蒙的。

389
00:36:44,080 --> 00:36:50,080
It is better to clean all glassware immediately after use with solvents of low toxicity,
最好在使用后立即用低毒性的溶剂清洗所有玻璃器皿，

390
00:36:50,080 --> 00:36:53,080
such as acetone or ethanol.
比如丙酮或乙醇。

391
00:36:53,080 --> 00:36:57,080
In this way, residues don't dry up and will be easier to remove.
这样残留物就不会干结，也更容易清除。

392
00:36:57,080 --> 00:37:03,080
Residue that is difficult to dissolve can be removed using bases or acids.
难以溶解的残留物可以用碱或酸去除。

393
00:37:06,740 --> 00:37:08,740
Look Smithy, this is what a flask should look like.
你看，Smithy，烧瓶就应该是这个样子。

394
00:37:08,740 --> 00:37:19,780
Then things with the reaction go smoothly, like with the gurneck's door.
这样反应就会进行得很顺利，就像上了发条一样。

395
00:37:19,780 --> 00:37:58,620
Now quickly put everything in the drain, then call it a day.
现在赶紧把所有东西都倒进下水道，然后收工。

396
00:37:58,620 --> 00:38:03,620
Whoever works with chemicals should also think about their appropriate disposal.
使用化学品的人也应该考虑如何妥善处置它们。

397
00:38:03,620 --> 00:38:07,620
Always remember, clean up as you go along.
始终记住，边做边清理。

398
00:38:07,620 --> 00:38:12,620
In a laboratory, there will be dangerous and toxic waste,
在实验室里，会产生危险和有毒的废物，

399
00:38:12,620 --> 00:38:17,620
which requires separate waste disposal to protect us and nature.
这些废物需要分开处置，以保护我们和自然。

400
00:38:17,620 --> 00:38:20,620
For this reason, there are special containers
因此，有专门的容器

401
00:38:20,620 --> 00:38:23,620
in which the waste is collected and disposed of.
用来收集和处置这些废物。

402
00:38:23,620 --> 00:38:25,620
How you should dispose of a chemical
一种化学品应该如何处置，

403
00:38:25,620 --> 00:38:28,620
can always be found in the safety information sheet.
总是可以在安全技术说明书中找到。

404
00:38:28,620 --> 00:38:38,470
Working in a laboratory is always potentially dangerous.
在实验室工作总是存在潜在危险。

405
00:38:38,470 --> 00:38:41,470
However, you should not be afraid,
不过，你不应该害怕，

406
00:38:41,470 --> 00:38:46,470
but work with concentration and the necessary respect for chemistry.
而是要集中注意力，对化学怀有必要的敬畏之心去工作。

407
00:38:46,470 --> 00:38:51,470
It is important to inform yourself about any dangers before commencing work.
重要的是在开始工作之前了解任何危险。

408
00:38:52,470 --> 00:38:57,470
And Smithy, if you had watched this little film before your lab course,
还有 Smithy，如果你在上实验课之前看过这部小影片，

409
00:38:57,470 --> 00:39:00,470
you would be in much better shape today.
你今天的状况就会好得多。
